{"seo":{"title":"Portfolio Site","description":"Testing phase of Portfolio Site."},"hero":{"headline":"Be Bored | Be Creative.","sub_headline":"// Architecting secure low-level logic","terminal_streams":["> USER_AUTH: Surya-Kaliappan","> Initializing Busy Protocol"],"resume_url":"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/Surya-Kaliappan/portfolio-data@master/resume.pdf?t=1783939207436"},"specs":[{"iconKey":"code-xml","title":"Practical Skill","value":"High","description":"With hands-on experience in web and Android development, I build applications focused on performance, scalability, and user experience."},{"iconKey":"disc","title":"Main Os","value":"Linux OS","description":"Command line over GUIs. Complete control over the bare metal. "},{"iconKey":"cpu","title":"Mindset","value":"Low-Level","description":"Manual memory management meets high-level network state. "}],"projects":[{"order_index":1,"num":"01","title":"Custom C++ Terminal Shell","stack":"C++, POSIX API, Linux System Calls","short_desc":"A fully functional, low-level UNIX shell engineered from scratch to directly interface with Linux kernel system calls and manage process lifecycles.","details":"Architected a custom command-line interpreter to master operating system concepts at the bare-metal level. This shell bypasses higher-level abstractions to read, parse, and execute user commands by interacting directly with POSIX API. It handles complex foreground and background process creation utilizing fork(), execvp(), and waitpid(). Furthermore, it features custom built-in commands (such as cd and typeof), manages signal interruptions (like SIGINT/Ctrl+c), and strictly handles memory allocation.","highlights":["Engineered a raw command parser that safely handles dynamic arguments and file descriptors.","Managed complex parent/child process lifecycles directly utilizing Linux System calls.","Implemented robust signal handling to gracefully catch and manage termination interrupts.","Built custom intrinsic commands to modify the shell's internal state environment."],"repo_link":"https://github.com/Surya-Kaliappan/shell-cpp"},{"order_index":2,"num":"02","title":"Chain of Custody Tracker","stack":"Hyperledger Fabric, Node.js, IPFS, MongoDB","short_desc":"A secure, immutable ledger system designed to track the lifecycle and handover of digital or physical assets without centralized vulnerability.","details":"Addressed the critical issue of data tampering in evidence and asset handling by utilizing permissioned blockchain technology. The application securely records every state chagne, timestampe, and ownership transfer into an immutable ledger. It ensures that only cryptographically authorized entities can endorse transactions, guaranteeing complete tracebility from an asset's origin to its final destination.","highlights":["Implemented permissioned ledger logic to securely track asset handovers and state changes.","Eliminated centralized database vulnerabilities by leveraging distributed peer endorsement."],"repo_link":"https://github.com/Surya-Kaliappan/chainOfCustody"},{"order_index":3,"num":"03","title":"Blockchain-Based Digital Agreement System","stack":"Hyperledger Fabric, IPFS, AES-256-GCM","short_desc":"A highly secure, decentralized platform for managing digital agreements, permissioned blockchain networks and encrypted off-chain storage","details":"Engineered as a comprehensive capstore project, this system ensures the integrity and privacy of digital contracts. It integrates digital signature for identity verification and utilized IPFS for decentralied document storage. Data payload security is strictly enforced using AES-256-GCM encryption, while Hyperledger Fabric manages the permissioned blockchain ledger and peer endorsement policies.","highlights":["Configured Hyperledger Fabric for complex peer endorsement logic","Integrated IPFS for immutable, decentralized file storage","Implemented AES-256-GCM encryption for secure payload transmission"],"repo_link":"https://github.com/Surya-Kaliappan/capestone"},{"order_index":4,"num":"04","title":"Facult Finder & Availability Architecture","stack":"React, React Native, Java, MySQL, Node.js","short_desc":"A real-time portal for students to locate faculty members, check live availability by schedule  to eliminate campus communication bottlenecks.","details":"Engineered a robust, full-stack ecosystem to solve systmic scheduling conflicts across the campus. The platform features a dual-role architecture for students and faculty. Students utilize a dynamic filtering system (by department, subject, designation) to find the current schedule of faculty. The backend is optimized to handle concurrent searching, managing race conditions and broadcasting real-time status updated to maintain absolute schedule integirty. and schedule has been maintain by Java Swing access only by administration. and end users can access via web and mobile application either.","highlights":["Implemented dynamic search algorithms to instantly filter facult by department, status and expertise.","Designed a robust centralized backend to handle request from different application.","Built java application to handle the database udpates and secured only for administration"],"repo_link":"https://github.com/Surya-Kaliappan/Faculty_Finder"},{"order_index":5,"num":"05","title":"Automated Certificate Generator","stack":"HTML, CSS, JavaScript","short_desc":"Tool generates certification with order name alignment in bulk to simplify certificate creation for educators and organizers.","details":"Developed a streamlined web utility to eliminate the manual data-entry bottleneck typically associated with event management. The tool allows users to upload raw participant data, which the system parses and perfectly aligns onto a customizable, high-resolution certificate template using HTML5 Canvas rendering. It efficiently batches the final outputs, solving the problem of generating hundreds of visually consistent certificates in secons.","highlights":["Built a highly efficient DOM rendering engine to dynamically align dynamic text over template images.","Solved manual data entry bottlenecks by iplementating bulk data processing and export logic."],"repo_link":"https://github.com/Surya-Kaliappan/certificate-generator"},{"order_index":6,"num":"06","title":"WebRTC Peer-to-Peer Network","stack":"WebRTC, PeerJS, JavaScript","short_desc":"A decentralized multiplayer application utilizing direct network-to-network connections without a central server.","details":"An eploration into decentralized network topology. This project leverages WebRTC and PeerJS to establish direct data channels between different devices across disparate networks. By eliinating the need for a central authoritative server, the application handles state reconciliation and message passing purely edge-to-edge","highlights":["Established direct peer-to-peer data channels across different networks.","Eliminated server bottlenecks using WebRTC for real-time state updates."],"repo_link":"https://github.com/Surya-Kaliappan/tic_tac_toe"},{"order_index":7,"num":"07","title":"Real-Time Quiz & Lobby Platform","stack":"React, Vite, Supabase, PostgreSQL","short_desc":"A live-syncing education platform featuring real-time student lobbies and state-driven session management.","details":"A full-stack application designed around instantaneous state synchronization. It utilizes Supabase's real-time edge function to cordinate multiple user views simultaneously. The core architecture relies on a strict state machine transitioning between 'Deploy', 'Active', and 'Reset' phases, ensuring the admin dashboard and student client interfaces remain perfectly synchronized.","highlights":["Architected a real-time lobby system using Supabase live edge function","Designed complex, multi-phase session synchronization"],"repo_link":"https://github.com/Surya-Kaliappan/quiz-um"}],"contact":{"status_text":"STANDBY","email_address":"kaliappansurya47@gmail.com","email_subject":"Inquiry: Connecting from Portfolio","email_body":"Hi Surya, I recently visited your portfolio and was impressed by your work. i would like to connect and discuss potential opportunities to collaborate. Looking forward to hearing from you.","social_links":[{"platform":"Github","url":"https://github.com/Surya-Kaliappan","iconKey":"link"}]}}